<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11630" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάτωρ</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[πᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>, ὁ, ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατήρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without father,</i> of deities, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτοπάτωρ, ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>H.</u>
					10.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. . . ἀμήτωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					41.53
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
				7.3
			</span></i>; <i>fatherless, orphan,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀοίκους ἀπάτοράς τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					300
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμήτωρ ἀ. τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					109
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πότμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>IT</u>
					864
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				103.35
			</span></i>: neut. pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάτορα τέκεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					114
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <i>disowned by the father,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				929a
			</span></i>: also c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐμοῦ</span>
			<i>not having</i> me <i>for a father,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1383
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of unknown father,</i>
			
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκότιος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.288e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PGrenf.</u>
				2.56.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
